  "summary": "github.com/crewjam/saml through v0.5.1 contains two vulnerabilities in SAML assertion processing:",
  "details": "github.com/crewjam/saml through v0.5.1 contains two vulnerabilities in SAML assertion processing:\n\n1. ServiceProvider.validateAssertion dereferences assertion.Issuer without a nil check when ExpectedIDPEntityID is non-empty. A signed SAML assertion that omits the optional <saml:Issuer> element causes a nil-pointer dereference panic after signature verification.\n\n2. Subject uses the bare XML struct tag xml:\"NameID\", which matches <NameID> elements in any XML namespace. When a signed assertion omits <saml:NameID> and includes a <NameID> element in a foreign namespace inside <saml:Subject>, encoding/xml populates Subject.NameID from the foreign element, allowing an authenticated principal to spoof Subject.NameID.Value.",
